course: dictionary
lesson: 1988
title: Words in context: compressor
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a new word from the words around it. These are its context, and they leave clues. «The humming you hear in the kitchen is the compressor switching on, and the quiet is it resting when the inside is cold enough.» Humming, switching on, resting and a cold inside all point to a machine, not a person.
explain: Another sentence says, «A pump called the compressor pushes a special liquid round pipes.» A pump is a machine that moves something, so compressor must be a machine too. Test your meaning by swapping it in: "the machine called the compressor pushes..." still makes sense.
explain: Look at the word's family. Compress means to squeeze something into a smaller space, so a compressor is a machine that squeezes. You do not need to know every word to understand a text; if the clues are not enough, check a dictionary.
fact: A compressor is a machine that squeezes air or gas into a smaller space.
fact: Squeezing a gas makes its pressure higher.
fact: Gases can be squashed, but liquids hardly can.
fact: Fridges, air conditioners and the pumps at garages all use compressors.
fact: In music, a compressor is a sound device that evens out loud and quiet parts.
exercise: «The humming you hear in the kitchen is the compressor switching on.» Where is the compressor most likely to be? | Under the sea | In a library book | *In a fridge
exercise: What does a compressor do to air or gas? | Makes it disappear completely | *Squeezes it into a smaller space | Paints it a bright colour
exercise: Which word is related to compressor? | candle | *compress | ladder
test: Why might a garage use an air compressor? | To cook a dinner | *To pump up tyres with squeezed air | To make rain fall | To fill car and bike tyres
test: What does a compressor do in music? | Writes the song's lyrics | *Evens out loud and quiet parts | Plays the drums faster
exam: Which statement about compressors is true? | They are always made of wood | *They squeeze gas into a smaller space | They make liquids disappear | They only play music
